        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9a1cfa0c-54cd-58a4-99ca-3908e91a5995",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carlton House, Carlton House Terrace, London\n- People: George IV, George III\n- Roles: Prince Regent, King of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, King of Hanover\n- Organizations: Crown Estate\n\nFacts:\n- George IV was born as George Augustus Frederick on 12 August 1762.\n- Carlton House was a mansion in London and became the town residence of the Prince Regent from 1783 for several decades.\n- From 1811 until his accession, George IV served as Prince Regent during the final mental illness of George III.\n- George III died on 29 January 1820, after which George IV became King of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland and of Hanover.\n- Carlton House Terrace replaced Carlton House, and the freehold of Carlton House Terrace still belongs to the Crown Estate.\n- George IV died on 26 June 1830.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
